DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261012T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261012T210000
SUMMARY:The Peculiar Worlds of Ransom Riggs: Step into Sunderworld and Miss
 
 Peregrine’s Home for Peculiar Children
LOCATION:The Masonic Lodge at Hollywood Forever\, Hollywood
DESCRIPTION:Join Chevalier's Books for a film screening and author event wi
 
th Ransom Riggs to celebrate the complete Sunderworld duology and the 10th 
 
anniversary of Tim Burton's Miss Peregrine's Home for Peculiar Children fil
 
m on Monday\, October 12 @ 7 PM at the Masonic Lodge at Hollywood Forever i
 
n Los Angeles\, CA. Q&A with Ransom Riggs and Tahereh Mafi to follow\, plus
 
 surprises\, and other peculiar fun! Ticket purchase includes a signed hard
 
copy of Sunderworld Vol. 1 or Sunderworld Vol. 2 and swag! Doors at 6:30PM 
 
Film Screening at 7PM RANSOM RIGGS is the #1 New York Times bestselling aut
 
hor of the Miss Peregrine's Peculiar Children novels. Riggs was born on a f
 
arm in Maryland and grew up in southern Florida. He studied literature at K
 
enyon College and film at the University of Southern California. He lives i
 
n Los Angeles with his wife\, bestselling author Tahereh Mafi\, and their f
 
amily.  TAHEREH MAFI is the #1 New York Times bestselling\, #1 internatio
 
nal bestselling\, and National Book Award-nominated author of over a dozen 
 
novels. Best known for the Shatter Me series\, her books have sold millions
 
 of copies\, and have been translated into over thirty languages. Her first
 
 contemporary novel\, A Very Large Expanse of Sea\, was named by Time magaz
 
ine as one of \, "rdquo" -> the best YA books of all time\," and is in deve
 
lopment for film with Levantine Films. She currently resides in Southern Ca
 
lifornia with her husband\, fellow author Ransom Riggs\, and their daughter
 
. Her most recent novel\, the second book in a new fantasy series\, These I
 
nfinite Threads\, is on shelves now. ABOUT TIM BURTON'S MISS PEREGRINE'S HO
 
ME FOR PECULIAR CHILDREN FILM ADAPTATION: When Jake (HUGO's Asa Butterfield
 
) discovers clues to a mystery that spans alternate realities and times\, h
 
e uncovers a secret refuge known as Miss Peregrine's Home for Peculiar Chil
 
dren. As he learns about the residents and their unusual abilities\, Jake r
 
ealizes that safety is an illusion\, and danger lurks in the form of powerf
 
ul\, hidden enemies -- and it's up to Jake to figure out who is real\, who 
 
can be trusted\, and who he really is. Featuring the ever-captivating Eva G
 
reen as the enigmatic Miss Peregrine\, the always great Samuel Jackson as a
 
n eerie villain\, plus a host of other notable peculiar talents including A
 
llison Janey\, Judi Dench\, Chris O'Dowd\, Rupert Everett\, and Terrance St
 
amp. _____________________________________________ ONSITE PARKING OPENS 1 H
 
OUR BEFORE DOORS PURCHASE ONSITE PARKING HERE Limit 4 tickets per household
 
 / customer / email / account / CC / address. Purchases that exceed the 4 t
 
icket limit are subject to cancellation. Orders placed for the sole purpose
 
 of resale may be cancelled without notice. The show will be held in a beau
 
tiful Masonic Lodge built in 1931. There are no elevators in this historic 
 
landmark. Ascending stairs is required to enter the venue. Tickets & info: 
 
https://hollywoodforever.com/event/the-peculiar-worlds-of-ransom-riggs-step
 
-into-sunderworld-and-miss-peregrines-home-for-peculiar-children/
URL:https://hollywoodforever.com/event/the-peculiar-worlds-of-ransom-riggs-
 
step-into-sunderworld-and-miss-peregrines-home-for-peculiar-children/
END:VEVENT
